WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.767
Take a closer look

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.668
now with

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.702
CNN military analyst

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.536
and retired Air Force

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.804
Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.905
Good to have you on, sir.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.407
So let's take a look at this mess.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.908
It looks very close

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:09.943
to the Ukrainian border.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.510
But to be frank,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.046
this is 25 miles inside

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.080
Russian territory.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.148
And as you know,

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.750
a lot of this territory here

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.617
is actually controlled

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.252
by Russian forces as well.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.987
So how surprising is a miss?

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.423
I imagine there was intended for a target

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.357
somewhere over here.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.592
It's quite surprising, Jim.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.127
And the reason it's so surprising

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.895
is that these aircraft,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.963
the SU 30,

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:33.099
34, is designed to go ahead and

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.802
and actually use a

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.504
be used as a stand off weapon.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.705
So as a standoff weapon,

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.873
it can use these missiles

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.208
to go attack targets very far away.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.045
When this weapon when this bomb came off,

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.713
it was probably a weapon

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.081
that was designed

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.015
in the old Soviet

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.217
era and had been modified

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.952
with GPS and wings.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.321
And as a result of that, those wings

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.890
probably failed to deploy.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.925
And instead of going straight forward

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:01.227
it went down and hit an intersection

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.262
right in the middle of Belgorod.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.696
The US has these help as well.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.597
They're called JDAMs.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.498
You basically put some,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.299
you know, wings on there

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:06.966
that you can control.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.068
So what you're saying, in effect,

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.036
it was meant to fire somewhere over here,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:10.870
stand off

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.338
or over the horizon

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.239
and instead

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.941
dropped on on Russian territory?

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.509
That's one possible scenario.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.610
The other scenario is that

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.512
it was a deliberate act

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.313
because it hit

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.481
right in the intersection

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.450
of a major street.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.618
And that is also kind of unusual,

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.286
to say the least.

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.054
And of course, that's a civilian target.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.389
And that's something that, you know,

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.890
should not have happened at all.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.891
Here's the other issue here,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.460
and this is a bigger picture problem

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.494
for Russian aircraft,

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.463
and that is that Ukrainian air defenses,

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.130
they're not perfect.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.198
We see bombs and missiles

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.599
dropping all the time,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.668
but they have effectively made

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.603
Ukrainian territory

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.239
a no fly zone for Russian aircraft

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.409
because the air defenses are significant

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:49.776
enough to

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:50.643
to put those pilots,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.112
those Russian pilots in danger.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.246
Is that a disadvantage

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.381
to Russian forces that they have to fire

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.716
from this side of the border in effect?

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:57.717
It is absolutely.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.985
Because if they were able

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.054
to have air supremacy over Ukraine,

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.755
they could fly anywhere

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.424
throughout the entire country

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.658
because they can't do that

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.861
because the systems are good enough

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.796
to prevent a lot of that flying.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.497
They did not achieve

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.164
air supremacy

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.932
or air superiority

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.367
throughout the entire airspace

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.435
of Ukraine.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:18.071
That means that this particular situation

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.973
could happen much more frequently.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.774
And it also means that the Russians

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.109
are at a considerable disadvantage

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:23.910
in targeting.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.411
They can target as accurately as they

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.846
otherwise would be able to listen.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.648
And as we said, it was a significant miss

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.450
that's the size of the crater there.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:30.984
But it's notable.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.018
Remember, early

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.520
on, the assessments were that

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.220
Russia would have to

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.355
establish superiority

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.923
or supremacy in the air

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.358
in the early stages of the war,

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.392
where more than a year later

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.727
and they haven't been able to do it.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.662
CNN's Nick Paton Walsh is live for us

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.030
in eastern Ukraine.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.065
Nick, what is the Kremlin saying about

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:46.733
what happened

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.436
Yeah, very little.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:50.870
And frankly,

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.471
apart from that,

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.406
this was essentially an accident

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.974
that is under investigation,

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.076
according to Russian state media.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.578
Obviously, deeply embarrassing

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.045
but perhaps

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.180
less embarrassing

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.080
than admitting

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.916
that this sort of explosion

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.850
may have been caused

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.685
by Ukrainian armed forces.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.452
This is an issue.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.087
34 strikes jets

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.222
its entirely unclear

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.056
whether the munition

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.891
simply fell off the aircraft

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.693
as it was flying over Belgorod

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.061
City to the northeast of Ukraine,

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.663
not far from its border,

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.531
or if there was some other mistaken

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.800
targeting or firing incident here.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.201
As you say,

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.303
it caused a significant crater

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.103
that a lot of damage

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.738
to the site of an apartment block,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.006
leaving one woman with brain

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.408
trauma head injuries

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.043
and another woman with lacerations

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.110
that were treated on the scene.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.312
Remarkable, frankly,

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.213
that it didn't kill

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.781
more Russian civilians.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.783
But also for those in Ukraine, often

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:40.053
the target of indiscriminate, inaccurate,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.322
appallingly judged indiscriminate

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.157
bombing against civilians.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.692
Little comfort to see it happen

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.160
to Russian citizens, too.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.928
But we are with some women

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:49.562
who've been sheltering

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.030
in a basement of an apartment

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.265
block for months

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.000
when they heard the news over the radio.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:54.534
And to them,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.301
they said it was the best thing

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.502
we had heard of in a while.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.338
But still an appalling sign of Russia's

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.906
military effectiveness.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.341
And Nick, the NATO's

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.509
secretary general is in Germany right now

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.411
meeting with Ukrainian officials.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.813
Jens Stoltenberg saying

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.582
that Ukraine's future is in NATO's.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:10.617
But he didn't give a

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:12.185
timeline for that, correct?

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:15.922
Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.190
And of
course, bear in mind

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.626
that Ukraine were to join NATO

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:20.994
while it's at war with Russia

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.362
would automatically

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.096
assume be trigger

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:23.763
Article five

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.864
and then NATO's would be part

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.299
of that war as well.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.767
And so a lengthy timeline

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.534
like clear heads

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.502
Ukraine's military

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.471
are rapidly equipped with NATO's

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.772
equipment is still far behind

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.907
the standards required to join NATO.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.276
But here is the sentiments

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:39.579
echoed by the NATO's chief

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:42.482
all needs

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.617
allies have agreed that Ukraine

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.453
will become a NATO member,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.291
but the main focus now is, of course,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:55.194
on the on how to ensure that Ukraine

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:56.596
prevails.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.900
Now, it's a very complex task.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.201
It requires unanimity across

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.403
all of NATO's members.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.171
It's even difficult to get Turkey

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:05.738
and Hungary

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.040
to fully sign on to Sweden

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:07.573
and Finland

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.309
too, aren't at war with Russia right now

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.810
to become part of NATO's.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.511
But the key point

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:12.945
there is not to be distracted

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.547
from the key task at hand,

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.149
and that is getting all the munitions

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:18.284
that Ukraine needs now, tanks,

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.086
anti-aircraft, to assist

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:20.920
with the forthcoming

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.288
Ukrainian counteroffensive

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.458
that many think maybe hours or days away.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.559
Back to you.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.393
Jan, Stoltenberg

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:27.960
also saying

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.761
he wants Ukraine's

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.763
military to be up to NATO's

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.633
grade of weapons and munitions, etc..

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.234
Nick Paton Walsh from Ukraine,

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.369
thank you so much for that report.

